.TH CAPRINT 1 "August 23, 2026" "VirtualSquare Labs"
.SH NAME
caprint \- print a process's ambient capability set
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B caprint
[
.B -c
|
.B -p
|
.B -l
]
[
.I pid
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B caprint
reads
.I /proc/pid/status
and displays its
.B CapAmb
set. Without a PID it reports its own process. A supplied PID must be a strict
positive decimal integer: signs, zero, overflow, and trailing text are rejected.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -c , " --compact"
Print a comma-separated line of short capability names.
.TP
.BR -p , " --prompt"
Print compact names followed by
.B #
for use in a shell prompt.
.TP
.BR -l , " --long"
Print the capability number, bit mask, and full libcap name.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print usage and exit.
.PP
The compact, prompt, and long formats are mutually exclusive.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cado (1),
.BR capabilities (7)
